#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:1
msgid "Source Installation on Ubuntu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:3
msgid "These instructions apply to Ubuntu Jammy (22.04)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:5
msgid "Install tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:7
msgid ""
"The use of some additional tools is recommended to help with the source "
"compilation, although other ways of correctly getting and building the "
"sources are also possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:10
msgid ""
"The easiest way to get the sources of all libraries is to use [vcstool]"
"(https://github.com/dirk-thomas/vcstool)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:13
msgid ""
"To compile all the different libraries and ign-gazebo in the right order "
"[colcon](https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/) is recommended. The "
"colcon tool is available on all platforms using pip (or pip3, if pip fails)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:17
msgid "Generic tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:19
msgid "Install tools needed by this tutorial:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:21
msgid "sudo apt install python3-pip lsb-release gnupg curl git\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:25
msgid "vcstool and colcon from pip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:27
msgid "PIP is available on all platforms:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:29
msgid "pip install vcstool || pip3 install vcstool\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:33
msgid ""
"pip install -U colcon-common-extensions || pip3 install -U colcon-common-"
"extensions\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:37
msgid ""
"Check that no errors were printed while installing with PIP. If your system "
"is not recognising the commands, and you're using a system that is "
"compatible with Debian or Ubuntu packages, see the instructions below to "
"install using `apt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:39
msgid ""
"After installing `vcstool` and `colcon` with PIP, you may need to add their "
"executables to your `$PATH`. Check where the installation of these packages "
"took place:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:42
msgid ""
"pip show vcstool || pip3 show vcstool | grep Location\n"
"\n"
"pip show colcon-common-extensions || pip3 show colcon-common-extensions | "
"grep Location\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:48
msgid ""
"If your install path is prefixed with `$HOME/.local`, you'll probably need "
"to add the executables within this directory to your `$PATH` in order to "
"avoid \"command not found\" errors when using `vcstool` and `colcon` later "
"on:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:50
msgid "export PATH=$PATH:$HOME/.local/bin/\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:54
msgid "vcstool and colcon from apt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:56
msgid ""
"An alternative method is to use the `.deb` packages available on Debian or "
"Ubuntu:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:58
msgid ""
"sudo curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ros/rosdistro/master/"
"ros.key -o /usr/share/keyrings/ros-archive-keyring.gpg\n"
"echo \"deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/"
"ros-archive-keyring.gpg] http://packages.ros.org/ros2/ubuntu $(lsb_release "
"-sc) main\" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ros2-latest.list > /dev/null\n"
"sudo apt-get update\n"
"sudo apt-get install python3-vcstool python3-colcon-common-extensions\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:65
msgid "Getting the sources"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:67
msgid ""
"The instructions below use some UNIX commands to manage directories but the "
"equivalent alternatives on Windows should provide the same result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:70
msgid ""
"The first step is to create a developer workspace in which `vcstool` and "
"`colcon` can work:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:73
msgid ""
"mkdir -p ~/workspace/src\n"
"cd ~/workspace/\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:78
msgid ""
"Use `vcstool` to automatically retrieve all the Ignition libraries sources "
"from their repositories:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:81
msgid ""
"vcs import --input https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ignition-tooling/"
"gazebodistro/master/collection-fortress.yaml src\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:85
msgid "The src subdirectory should contain all the sources ready to be built."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:87
msgid "Install dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:89
msgid ""
"Before compiling it is necessary to install all the dependencies of the "
"different packages that compose the Fortress collection. Every platform has "
"a different method to install software dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:93
msgid "Add `packages.osrfoundation.org` to the apt sources list:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:95
msgid ""
"sudo curl https://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo.gpg --output /usr/share/"
"keyrings/pkgs-osrf-archive-keyring.gpg\n"
"echo \"deb [arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture) signed-by=/usr/share/keyrings/"
"pkgs-osrf-archive-keyring.gpg] http://packages.osrfoundation.org/gazebo/"
"ubuntu-stable $(lsb_release -cs) main\" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/"
"gazebo-stable.list > /dev/null\n"
"sudo apt-get update\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:101
msgid ""
"The command below must be run from a workspace with the Gazebo source code "
"and will install all dependencies in Ubuntu:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:103
msgid ""
"cd ~/workspace/src\n"
"sudo apt -y install \\\n"
"  $(sort -u $(find . -iname 'packages-'`lsb_release -cs`'.apt' -o -iname "
"'packages.apt' | grep -v '/\\.git/') | sed '/ignition\\|sdf/d' | tr '\\n' ' "
"')\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:109
msgid "Install compiler requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:111
msgid ""
"The Ignition Libraries require the gcc compiler version 8 or higher. "
"(Windows requires Visual Studio 2019)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:114
msgid "The default compiler in Ubuntu Jammy already meets this requirement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:116
msgid "Building the Ignition Libraries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:118
msgid ""
"Once the compiler and all the sources are in place it is time to compile "
"them. Start the procedure by changing into the workspace and listing the "
"packages recognized by `colcon`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:122
msgid ""
"cd ~/workspace/\n"
"colcon graph\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:127
msgid ""
"`colcon graph` should list the Ignition libraries with an [interdependency "
"diagram](https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/reference/verb/"
"graph.html#example-output). If that is the case, then you are ready to build "
"the whole set of libraries:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:132
msgid "colcon build --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:136
msgid "To speed up the build process, you could also disable tests by using"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:138
msgid "colcon build --cmake-args -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF --merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:142
msgid ""
"To use debuggers activate debug symbols. Gazebo will run slower, but you'll "
"be able to use GDB:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:144
msgid ""
"colcon build --cmake-args ' -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF' ' -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug' "
"--merge-install\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:148
msgid "To build a specific package with all its dependent packages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:150
msgid "colcon build --merge-install --packages-up-to PACKAGE_NAME\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:154
msgid "To build a single package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:156
msgid "colcon build --packages-select PACKAGE_NAME\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:160
msgid ""
"Visit [colcon documentation](https://colcon.readthedocs.io/en/released/#) to "
"view more `colcon` build and test options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:162
msgid ""
"If there are no errors, all the binaries should be ready to use. You can "
"check the [Troubleshooting] section for errors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:164
msgid "Using the workspace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:166
msgid "The workspace needs to be sourced every time a new terminal is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:168
msgid "Run the following command to source the workspace in bash:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:170
msgid ". ~/workspace/install/setup.bash\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:174
msgid "Or in zsh:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:176
msgid ". ~/workspace/install/setup.zsh\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:180
msgid ""
"This is the end of the source install instructions; head back to the "
"[Getting started](getstarted) page to start using Ignition!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:183
msgid "Uninstalling source-based install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:185
msgid ""
"A source-based install can be \"uninstalled\" using several methods, "
"depending on the results you want:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:188
msgid ""
"If you installed your workspace with `colcon` as instructed above, "
"\"uninstalling\" could be just a matter of opening a new terminal and not "
"sourcing the workspace's `setup.sh`. This way, your environment will behave "
"as though there is no Ignition install on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:193
msgid ""
"If, in addition to not wanting to use the libraries, you're also trying to "
"free up space, you can delete the entire workspace directory with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:196
msgid "rm -rf ~/workspace\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:200
msgid ""
"If you want to keep the source code, you can remove the `install` / "
"`build` / `log` directories as desired, leaving the `src` directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:203
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../install_ubuntu_src.md:205
msgid "See [Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md#ubuntu)"
msgstr ""
